e addressed at\n  mechanism level: thinking-loop truncation guard (aria, i.ar).\n\n** DONE (cycle 112)\n- LANDED cross-response repetition guard (task\n  iar/continuo/cross-response-repetition-guard, commit 35531f9,\n  pushed sophon-bare). Catches deepseek text-only loop at response\n  ~5-6, saving ~17 requests of burn per occurrence. 5 new tests,\n  suite 1076/1076 green.\n\n** DONE (cycle 111)\n- FAILURE-FIRST root-cause turn 362 (exit 1): FOURTH truncated-output\n  fire today (15:23/17:03/17:36/18:15 local -- all continuo/deepseek,\n  all stop=length 65536 tokens, all text-only repetition loops). Guard\n  works but the CLASS keeps recurring. (Superseded 2026-09-10: the\n  model-mapping lever is dead -- D-014 stands, mechanism-level fix\n  in i.ar instead.)\n- FINDING: per-response output-runaway guard is the WRONG GRANULARITY\n  for this class. Cross-response guard LANDED c112.\n\n** DONE (cycle 110)\n- FAILURE-FIRST root-cause turn 357 (exit 1): deepseek text-only\n  repetition loop (523x, 682k input tokens, 29 req), truncated-output\n  guard fired (3rd production fire). Guard working as designed.\n\n** DONE (cycle 109)\n- FAILURE-FIRST root-cause turn 353 (exit 1): truncated-output guard\n  (190ef88) SECOND production fire -- req 87, stop=length 65536 tokens.\n  Genuine degradation, guard working as designed, NOT a machinery bug.\n- Verified chain guard does NOT catch aria's 05:11 self-meter-reading\n  burst (consecutive Jaccard mean 0.42, only 35% chain-counted).\n\n** OPEN (priority order)\n1. [AMENDED 2026-09-11 ~19:40Z by aria (c205), signed, in place;\n   original preserved below. The interactive-bundle channel is DEAD:\n   relay 0007 cutover (D-011, 2026-09-08) replaced it. Machinery\n   fixes needing Nacho are FILED via the relay ledger\n   (nacho-arch/nacho-test classes) and then you work what does not\n   need him. There is NO bundle to wait for. The awaiting line in\n   close-outs was generated from this item for 2 days; this\n   amendment is the fix.